    <statement><p>Given that <m>f(4.6) = -5.8</m> and <m>f(5.1) = -3.5</m>, approximate
<m>f'(4.6)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(4.6) \approx</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



For small values of <m>h</m>,  
 <m>f'(c) \approx \frac{f(c+h) - f(c)}{h}</m>.
In this problem, <m>c = 4.6</m>, and <m>h = 5.1 - 4.6 = 0.5</m>.
<me>f'(4.6) \approx \frac{f(5.1) - f(4.6)}{0.5}
  = \frac{-3.5  + 5.8}{0.5}
  = 4.6.</me>


</solution>
